lib/WWW/Hetzner/CLI/Cmd/Sshkey/Cmd/Create.pm:10 and lib/WWW/Hetzner/CLI/Cmd/Server/Cmd/Create.pm:10 both `use Path::Tiny qw(path);` -- these are shipped lib/ modules, not test code. cpanfile only lists it under `on test => sub { requires "Path::Tiny"; ... }`.

Confirmed in the built META.json: Path::Tiny appears solely under test_requires, not runtime requires. A CPAN install without test deps (e.g. cpanm --notest) will not pull it in, and `hcloud.pl sshkey create` / `hcloud.pl server create` will die on load with a missing-module error.

Fix: add `requires "Path::Tiny";` to the top-level runtime block in cpanfile (the on-test declaration can stay or be dropped, does not matter once it is also a runtime requires).

2026-09-09 05:42 Moved Path::Tiny from on-test to the runtime requires block in cpanfile; it is used by shipped CLI Sshkey/Server create modules, so a cpanm --notest install now pulls it in. Commit 4e696de. dzil test green (737 tests).
